title: DuFour's Resistance Crumbles...
subtitle: The pressure begins to mount on the President.
view-if: chancellor = "Staal" and staal_time == 7 and staal_explode
new-page: true
tags: event
priority: -4
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: imperial_collusion += 1
on-display: {!  
    var cardEl = document.createElement('div');  
    cardEl.className = "face-figure2";  

    var image = new Image();  
    image.className = "face-img";  
    image.src = "img/hindie.jpg";  

    cardEl.appendChild(image);
    var contentDiv = document.querySelector("#page #mid_panel #content");
    contentDiv.appendChild(cardEl);
!}

= Negotiations, Pt. 2

With his closest friends, his nephew, and his chief of staff all advocating for a [+ royalist_chancellor +] chancellorship, DuFour’s once-unshakable resolve to refuse [+ royalist_chancellor +] is beginning to crumble. It is not only their pressure that wears at him: his faith in the Commonwealth’s quarrelsome institutions has worn thin, and beneath it the old Imperial loyalties of his youth stir anew.

In the long sleepless nights he has begun to reason his way toward the unthinkable. The Empress is coming—if not this year then the next; the frontier cannot hold a republic this brittle forever. Better, then, a chancellor who speaks the Crown's language and can meet the Empress's court as something other than a supplicant. He no longer tells himself it is temporary. He tells himself only that every road now leads north to the same gate—and that this one, at least, he might yet hope to steer.

- @nazi_2

@nazi_2
title: DuFour receives a visit from an old friend.
on-arrival: dufour_gallax_r += 1

Elric Hartwell, the elderly *noble* neighbor of the President in East Heartland—and the man who once rallied the Commonwealth Right to buy DuFour's estate as a gift in 4292—arrives with advice. He assures the President that only a [+ royalist_chancellor +] cabinet can bring relief to the depressed agriculture of the east, and that conservative forces would be enough to prevent a one-party dictatorship.

- @nazi_3

@nazi_3
title: DuFour receives a reassuring message from Gorrick.
on-arrival: dufour_gallax_r += 1

Gorrick, a decorated war hero and fellow officer, sends a message pledging respect for DuFour’s authority as President. He insists his party has no intention of violating the constitution or politicizing the military—words that make an impression on the President.

- @nazi_4

@nazi_4
title: His resolve begins to fail.
on-arrival: dufour_gallax_r += 1

In a meeting with Goodryke, the former Chancellor presents [+ royalist_chancellor +] in a moderate light, claiming he only seeks a minimal number of cabinet positions and is willing to submit the remaining appointments for the President's approval. Goodryke also reports that many ministers from his and Staal’s cabinets are prepared to continue under [+ royalist_chancellor +]. Despite his dislike of Mallin, DuFour agrees to grant him control of both the national[? if heartland_leader == "Staal":&nbsp;and Heartland?] ministries of agriculture and economics.

DuFour is also offered the choice of appointing the Foreign and Defense Ministers. He is pleased to learn that the aristocratic Foreign Minister from Goodryke and Staal’s cabinet is willing to remain under [+ royalist_chancellor +]. As for the Defense Ministry, it is agreed Staal must go. DuFour proposes General Konrad Halloran—currently serving with the Commonwealth delegation in Vera and a known rival of Staal within the ministry.

Goodryke ends the meeting by promising to serve as Vice-Chancellor. The day ends, and the next begins.